{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The express Effective Date supplies the date intended by the introductory immediate-effect language.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected formal control excludes applications caught by the transition, because their treatment requires the existing process and missing FAQs.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The introductory reference to home supervision describes the measures' purpose; it is not treated as an additional independently specified condition in item (ii).","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"3ba4bde717985a09f564d0eff99c12ebad94a746720bac76452ef3844383c5a0","candidate_id":"candidate.c58c1ea10da24828ab5a78d536c4cad0","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for a material UCITS investment change outside the legacy-application transition. Within the stated scope, true means the change meets the circular's stated home-compliance condition and none of its stated exceptions applies. False means this removal is unavailable under those conditions; it does not independently establish a prohibition, non-compliance or the complete underlying approval obligation. Outside scope, the result supplies no determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.38de7a092ede4fa6adb46eca7e49604c","issue.d875fa172f6646fe82aa7e8818ad2932","issue.99caf060a70f41de84d2d18a46f52d45"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The text supports a clear removal-of-approval eligibility rule for changes outside the transition, rather than rival conjunctive and disjunctive exception rules. For example, an ordinary home-compliant investment-policy change in a covered Irish UCITS after the Effective Date qualifies if it has no possible local policy implications; the same change with possible local policy implications does not qualify even if it is neither novel nor complex. For an otherwise identical application received on 27 November 2025 and pending at transition, existing processing applies and this formal control gives no answer. The strongest uncertainty is whether that preserved processing also necessarily preserves the substantive approval prerequisite.","run_id":"run.0f2ce1078fce4ae886d5596a4951f0ba","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"6c557525c251e4c0794c0061ba5b7f7fec9be45d9495dd1ca07063f018b43c06","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556","d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Prior-approval removal for material changes to UCITS investment objectives, policies or restrictions"}